WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.216
The school reading index names eleven Week 15 rows: homeostasis, BCEHS A05, BCPEG abbreviations/load/transport, hypertension/encephalopathy, scope/resource coordination, fall prevention, leadership/collaboration, triage pacing, legal considerations and emergency measurement order.
学校阅读索引列出第15周十一项：稳态、BCEHS A05、BCPEG缩写/装载/转运、高血压/脑病、执业范围/资源协调、跌倒预防、领导/协作、检伤节奏、法律考量和紧急测量顺序。

00:00:24.216 --> 00:00:40.128
Nancy Caroline Canadian eighth edition is an additional learner-confirmed exam text. Its selected Chapter 50 MCI/incident-command material supports the week, but it is not a twelfth school row and cannot replace the listed books.
Nancy Caroline加拿大第八版是学习者确认的额外考试主教材。其第50章多伤员事件/事件指挥选读可支持本周学习，但不是学校第十二项阅读，也不能替代清单中的教材。

00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:59.064
The school PDFs now support the eleven connected readers below. Their coverage follows the actual assigned ranges and named topics, not just the short labels in the index. Fundamentals covers both complete spans: evidence-based research and collaboration, then leadership and management.
以下十一份相连的阅读讲解现已依据学校PDF编写，范围遵循真实指定页段和点名主题，不只讲索引中的简短标签。Fundamentals完整覆盖两段：循证研究与协作，以及领导与管理。

00:00:59.064 --> 00:01:24.768
Two page locators still cannot be verified: cardiovascular page two hundred thirty-nine and BCPEG page one hundred forty-nine. Study the actual hypertension chapter and the verified abbreviations and transport pages, but do not treat those as proof that the missing pages were found. The CPSC reader separately explains literal transfer pages and the named fall-prevention section.
两项页码仍无法核实：心血管教材第239页及BCPEG第149页。应学习真实高血压章节、已核缩写页和装载转运页，但不能据此声称找到了缺页。CPSC阅读另行区分字面指定的转移页面与点名的跌倒预防部分。

00:01:24.768 --> 00:01:41.544
For a physiology row, write the feedback mechanism and one observable system change. For an operations row, write the role, report and patient-flow purpose. For a legal row, record the jurisdiction and current authority before applying it.
生理学阅读要记录反馈机制及一项可观察的系统变化；操作阅读要记录角色、通报和患者流动目标；法律阅读则应先记录司法辖区和现行权威，再考虑应用。

00:01:41.544 --> 00:01:54.720
This matters especially for MCI: an old generic algorithm or a nursing role description is not the same as the current BCEHS job aid or PCP licence. Keep the source named beside the note.
这对多伤员事件尤其重要：通用旧算法或护理角色说明，不等同于BCEHS现行工作卡或PCP执照范围。笔记旁应标明来源名称。

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:11.424
MCI studies may describe tourniquets, airway actions, transport systems, nursing assessment and hospital distribution. A reading assignment alone does not authorize an individual action, broaden a licence or override the current incident plan.
多伤员教材可能介绍止血带、气道操作、转运系统、护理评估和医院分流。仅有阅读任务不能授权个人操作、扩大执照范围或覆盖现行事件计划。

00:02:11.424 --> 00:02:25.152
Use the current Emergency Medical Assistants Regulation, BCEHS guidance and service procedures for operational boundaries. The school’s timed skill is a learning target, not permission for unsupervised practice.
操作边界应依据现行《Emergency Medical Assistants Regulation》、BCEHS指导和服务流程。学校计时技能是学习目标，不是无人监督操作的许可。

00:02:25.152 --> 00:02:48.360
The learner-confirmed Nancy Canadian eighth edition indexes Chapter 50, Medical Incident Command, with sections on disasters, MCI, ICS, paramedic response, medical incident command and triage. The supplied PDF corpus supports Chapter 50 at physical PDF pages 4155-4194.
學習者確認的Nancy加拿大第八版在第50章“Medical Incident Command”列出災害、多傷員事件、ICS、院前救援響應、醫療事件指揮和檢傷等部分。所提供PDF語料把第50章定位於物理PDF頁4155至4194。

00:02:48.360 --> 00:03:03.936
Use that chapter for the broader logic of coordination, roles, tagging and dynamic reassessment. Older textbook language may use different triage labels or thresholds; the current BCEHS adult and pediatric charts govern the skill practice.
可用該章理解協同、分工、標記和動態再評估的整體邏輯。較舊教材可能使用不同檢傷名稱或閾值；技能練習應遵循BCEHS成人及兒童現行圖表。
